XWEB-204: Fixed sitemap and blog RSS 500 errors

Problem identified:
- Apache htaccess catch-all rewrite was redirecting XML file requests to index.html
- React app attempted to handle these routes and failed with 500 errors
- Affected sitemap.xml and blogg/rss.xml

Solution implemented:
- Added MIME type declarations for XML files in public/.htaccess
- Added rewrite exception for xml and txt files before catch-all SPA redirect
- Ensures static XML files generated during build are served correctly

Testing completed:
- Build passes successfully
- All 989 tests pass
- Lint and typecheck pass
- Verified sitemap.xml and rss.xml are generated with valid XML content

Pull request created:
- PR #128: https://github.com/xalatechnologies/xala-web-cloner/pull/128
- Branch: cursor/fix-sitemap-rss-500-60f2
- Status: Ready for review
- Single commit with clear explanation of changes

After deployment:
- Crawlers will receive 200 OK for sitemap.xml requests
- Crawlers will receive 200 OK for blogg/rss.xml requests
- Both files will have proper Content-Type headers
- robots.txt continues pointing to correct sitemap URL
